From fb6554d67d06f80d726f45582c8bb062912b7679 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 06:58:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: an image beside its tool result carries the turn
 (#5767)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

pi sends a tool's picture in a user message after its text-only tool
message ("Attached image(s) from tool result:"). turnIn read that
message as the user's next ask — an image of theirs begins a turn —
and ended the turn there. The bridge reads it as the result's, and
hands the picture to the waiting run (match); the router, told the
turn was over, stopped keeping the conversation to the account that
answered it, and re-decided it per request. When the pick landed on
another account, the bridge let the run go — another account's Claude
Code must not spend its quota — and a new one was told the whole
conversation: "tool results account changed", the fixed prefix read
from the cache, everything after it written again, at each of the
session's image reads. The same results as text carry no picture
message, the turn held, and nothing restarted.

An image beside the turn's results now carries the turn on, as the
bridge tells it; the user's own image with no result of the turn's
waiting still begins one. And when a changed owner still lets a run
go, the log names both sides — "account changed: the run was on
claude (a@example.com), this request goes to claude (b@example.com)",
own sign-ins and plan-named accounts marked — instead of a bare
"account changed" that left the reporter guessing at image hashes.

Ablation: with the carries-the-turn case out,
TestTurnInCarriesAnImageBesideItsToolResult fails at "turn 2 within
false, want 1 true" — the reporter's shape. Whole, it passes, and
the user's own image still counts a turn.

Run at upstream/main e3ab7f3bf + this commit, macOS 15 (darwin/arm64):
TestTurnIn*, TestToolResultsNameTheChangedOwner, the turn/affinity/
bridge family, and internal/gateway whole (-tags nogui, 826s) ok.
